# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This directory is the public source repository (GPLv3). Everything not
# ignored here becomes public, so this file is a safety boundary, not just
# housekeeping — read docs/LICENSING.md (kept private) before loosening it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets. Never relax these. ------------------------------------------
# The example file (keystore.properties.example) is checked in; the real one
# is not. `local.properties` is matched without a leading slash on purpose:
# the upstream rule anchored it to this directory and missed app/local.properties.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
keystore.properties
signing.properties
local.properties
google-services.json
.env

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
build/
.gradle/
captures/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
.cxx/
app/app/.cxx/

# --- Prebuilt binaries -----------------------------------------------------
# The AARs and .so files are build products, not source. GPL asks for the
# source they are built from, and that is what cores/ and the vendored trees
# carry. Shipping the binaries as well would only make the repo heavy and let
# a stale artefact disagree with the source beside it.
*.aar
*.aar.*
app/app/libs/**/*.so
app/app/libs/*/hev-socks5-tunnel-bin

# --- Cloned, not vendored --------------------------------------------------
# Upstream MIT source, unmodified, with its own submodules. Kept out for the
# same reason the sing-box tree is: a pinned commit and a clone command say the
# same thing without carrying somebody else's repository inside ours. Its
# licence obliges a notice, not redistribution. See the README for the pin.
hev-socks5-tunnel/

# --- Not built from here ---------------------------------------------------
# A leftover clone from a feasibility test. Nothing in the build references it
# and libv2ray.aar is a prebuilt upstream release — see the README. Left on
# disk, kept out of the repo so nobody mistakes it for the source we build.
AndroidLibXrayLite/

# --- IDE and OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Noise -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp
